### Design Rationale Summary

| Task | Rule Type | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| **find hopper** | `position_near_with_facing` | This is a find/locate task — the preferred rule type checks that the player navigated near the hopper (at spawn-relative 5,0,5) and is facing it. max_distance=16 is generous enough for natural discovery, facing_tolerance=60° ensures the player is actually looking at it. |
| **craft to stone_pickaxe** | `inventory_has` | Crafting tasks → inventory_has (top preference). The crafted stone_pickaxe ends up in inventory. Player starts with empty inventory so no false positives. |
| **mine gray_concrete** | `inventory_has` | Mining tasks → inventory_has (top preference). Gray concrete drops itself when mined with a pickaxe. The item appears in inventory. Player starts with no gray_concrete so no false positives. |

All three milestones use the simplest, most direct rule type per the preference hierarchy. No unnecessary spatial constraints are added to the crafting or mining tasks.
